# %% [markdown]
# 
# ### NLP with Disaster Tweets — Real Disaster vs. Figurative Language
#
# **Domain:** Social Media / Civic
#
# **Problem Statement:** During disasters, emergency services are overwhelmed with
# social media data. This notebook builds an NLP classifier that identifies **real
# disaster tweets** from **figurative ones** (e.g. "this exam was a disaster") to
# help emergency teams triage social media faster.
#
# **Dataset:** Kaggle — [NLP with Disaster Tweets](https://www.kaggle.com/c/nlp-getting-started)
# (7,613 labeled tweets: `id`, `keyword`, `location`, `text`, `target`)
#
# **Pipeline (required core approach):**
# 1. Clean tweets using regex (remove URLs, hashtags, mentions)
# 2. Tokenize and preprocess using NLTK (stopwords + lemmatization)
# 3. TF-IDF vectorization
# 4. Train SVM / Logistic Regression **+ Naive Bayes, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting** for comparison
# 5. Evaluate using F1-score, confusion matrix, ROC-AUC, and 5-fold cross-validation
#
# ---

